WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.350
- Say hi to the Fireman.

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:02.436
It's their first time here in America.

00:00:02.436 --> 00:00:03.269
- Hi

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:04.792
- Hi Firemen

00:00:04.792 --> 00:00:05.625
- Oh wow.

00:00:05.625 --> 00:00:06.458
- We, we noticed you.

00:00:06.458 --> 00:00:07.291
- Yeah.

00:00:07.291 --> 00:00:08.790
Billy joked backstage

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:10.870
that I wore the same
outfit as you guys did.

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:12.240
- He technically did.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:13.740
- Yeah. But I've never been a Fireman.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:15.640
I just played one in a Hallmark movie.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:17.760
- So it's basically the same, right?

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:18.800
- No, no, not at all.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:21.030
It requires the same level of bravery.

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:21.863
- Yes.

00:00:21.863 --> 00:00:23.280
- Did you ever, cause my son, he's six

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:24.900
he's gone through the phase
that he wanted to be a fireman.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.760
Did y'all ever wanna be a
Fireman when you were a kid?

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.890
- Yeah. They're like, you know

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:31.084
the greatest heroes in
our society, you know?

00:00:31.084 --> 00:00:34.783
- Yeah.

00:00:34.783 --> 00:00:35.820
- Aww, that's sweet.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.410
I like that. I like that.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:39.060
Well, wait, I know that
we've talked before

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:40.950
about your parents and how
much they encouraged you

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:41.970
you know, and that's so cool.

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:42.803
The entertainment world.

00:00:42.803 --> 00:00:44.250
Yeah. So did they, I don't know.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.540
How were they like when you were a kid?

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:47.086
Cause you sing in this

00:00:47.086 --> 00:00:47.919
- I do.

00:00:47.919 --> 00:00:48.752
- And I have to lead with this

00:00:48.752 --> 00:00:49.585
cause I'm a singer or whatever.

00:00:49.585 --> 00:00:50.776
- Yes.

00:00:50.776 --> 00:00:51.609
- You're a singer?

00:00:51.609 --> 00:00:52.740
- What? I know.

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:54.840
No, but I just, I had to lead
with it cause I thought it

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:57.120
was so great at the end
when you were singing.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:58.295
- Thank you.

00:00:58.295 --> 00:00:59.349
I was like, I'm sorry Billy.

00:00:59.349 --> 00:01:00.647
I didn't know that about you.

00:01:00.647 --> 00:01:02.820
- That a big compliment coming from you.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:04.853
No, it's such great tone, you're vibrato.

00:01:04.853 --> 00:01:05.786
- Thank you.

00:01:05.786 --> 00:01:06.619
- (Kelly)Yeah.

00:01:06.619 --> 00:01:07.452
- Wow. Okay.

00:01:07.452 --> 00:01:08.445
- We're talking technique.

00:01:08.445 --> 00:01:09.278
- I know.

00:01:09.278 --> 00:01:10.530
When I was a kid I opened my mouth

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:12.279
as a young boy and had
a good singing voice.

00:01:12.279 --> 00:01:13.112
- (Kelly)Yeah.

00:01:13.112 --> 00:01:15.109
- And I grew up in New York City

00:01:15.109 --> 00:01:16.980
and I was really lucky cause
my parents loved Broadway.

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:18.510
So they took me to a lot of Broadway.

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:19.770
They took me to see concerts

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:20.696
and they really encouraged me to sing.

00:01:20.696 --> 00:01:21.529
- How lucky.

00:01:21.529 --> 00:01:22.417
- I was so lucky.

00:01:22.417 --> 00:01:23.250
- Yeah.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:24.083
- Yeah.

00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:25.650
And it was a, I think
that's why I'm here today

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:27.120
because they were so supportive.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:27.953
Mm. Yeah.

00:01:27.953 --> 00:01:28.786
- I love that.

00:01:28.786 --> 00:01:30.210
- Speaking of music, I found out

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:32.216
that you're like a huge Garth Brooks fan.

00:01:32.216 --> 00:01:33.049
- I am.

00:01:33.049 --> 00:01:33.882
For real.

00:01:33.882 --> 00:01:36.045
And that actually ties into
our movie a little bit.

00:01:36.045 --> 00:01:36.878
- I know.

00:01:36.878 --> 00:01:38.850
So that's where the dance,
you're doing the dance, isn't it?

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:40.055
Like it's a different layer.

00:01:40.055 --> 00:01:40.908
- It's an homage to the dance.

00:01:40.908 --> 00:01:41.773
- Yes.

00:01:41.773 --> 00:01:42.606
- That I see.

00:01:42.606 --> 00:01:43.440
- I recognized the song--

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:44.273
- Yes, yes.

00:01:44.273 --> 00:01:45.106
- The melody. Yeah.

00:01:45.106 --> 00:01:45.939
- Which you sang--

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:46.772
- Brilliantly.

00:01:46.772 --> 00:01:47.881
- You're version of the
dance was absolutely.

00:01:47.881 --> 00:01:49.381
- Oh, at the Kennedy Center, thank you.

00:01:49.381 --> 00:01:50.214
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:50.214 --> 00:01:51.387
- You made Garth Brooks cry

00:01:51.387 --> 00:01:52.220
- (Kelly) Aw, thank you.

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:53.220
- And everybody watching you.

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:54.725
- I watched that like 30 times.

00:01:54.725 --> 00:01:55.558
- (Kelly) Thank you.

00:01:55.558 --> 00:01:58.020
- Literally during the
filming we were talking a lot

00:01:58.020 --> 00:01:59.070
about Garth Brooks

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:02.280
and and Billy actually wrote that song

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:03.491
during the filming of it.

00:02:03.491 --> 00:02:04.324
- Oh, really?

00:02:04.324 --> 00:02:05.157
It was not something
that was totally planned.

00:02:05.157 --> 00:02:06.155
- Yeah.

00:02:06.155 --> 00:02:07.080
- It came out of a conversation
that we had about --

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:08.215
- Yeah.

00:02:08.215 --> 00:02:09.048
- What music we like.

00:02:09.048 --> 00:02:09.881
- Yeah. Because we didn't

00:02:09.881 --> 00:02:11.446
know each other before
we started shooting.

00:02:11.446 --> 00:02:12.279
- (Kelly) Yeah.

00:02:12.279 --> 00:02:13.860
- And we were trying to
get to know each other.

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:16.080
So I said to him, you know,
what kind of music do you like?

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:17.850
And he said, actually
I love country music.

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:20.010
And my favorite singer is Garth Brooks.

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:22.650
And I was thinking my character
in the movie at the end

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:24.181
I don't want to give it
all away, but you know

00:02:24.181 --> 00:02:26.539
he needs to make a grand gesture.

00:02:26.539 --> 00:02:27.372
- (Kelly) Yeah.

00:02:27.372 --> 00:02:28.500
- You know, cause he's
in love with this guy

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:30.030
but has a hard time expressing himself.

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:30.863
We both do.

00:02:30.863 --> 00:02:32.580
That's what Bros is about.

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:35.610
And I thought, you know
what I, I like the idea

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:39.420
of a gay man singing a Garth
Brooks inspired country song,

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:42.060
a love song, to the guy he's in love with.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:43.950
Even though my character
doesn't love country music

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:44.783
but his does.

00:02:44.783 --> 00:02:46.740
So that's part of the gesture.

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:47.573
- Yeah.

00:02:47.573 --> 00:02:48.750
- You have great taste in real life.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:49.767
I'm just saying.

00:02:49.767 --> 00:02:50.800
- (Billy)Thank you very much.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:51.840
- I, I noticed you liked country

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:53.370
so I gave you George Strait vinyl.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:54.203
- Yes.

00:02:54.203 --> 00:02:55.066
- Just saying, dip into that.

00:02:55.066 --> 00:02:57.398
- Absolutely. Amarillo By Morning.

00:02:57.398 --> 00:02:58.231
Oh yes.

00:02:58.231 --> 00:02:59.177
- (Kelly)Oh my gosh. Its so good.

00:02:59.177 --> 00:03:00.540
- He's a real country fan.

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:02.190
- I actually tried to play
it on your record player.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:03.720
Your record player
backstage was not working.

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:04.716
- It was not working.

00:03:04.716 --> 00:03:05.549
It was not working for me.

00:03:05.549 --> 00:03:08.310
- We like to just give
you the vinyl to look at.

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:11.490
- Oh, well I took it out cause
I wanted to get it going.

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:12.630
- We will now fix that.

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:13.463
- Uh, yes.

00:03:13.463 --> 00:03:14.296
Heads will roll at the
Kelly Clarkson Show.

00:03:14.296 --> 00:03:16.771
- No, no, no, they're like,
what was wrong with the needle?

00:03:16.771 --> 00:03:17.806
Anyway, so like what

00:03:17.806 --> 00:03:20.580
musical artist did you
grow up listening to?

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:22.860
- I'm a little different, you
know, that's what's great.

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:25.048
He was a, a gay guy that
loved country music.

00:03:25.048 --> 00:03:29.250
I grew up in New York City,
you know, I loved Madonna.

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:32.970
You know, I, I loved Barbara Streisand.

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:34.711
My parents took me to
see Barbara Streisand.

00:03:34.711 --> 00:03:35.544
- Oh, you've seen her live?

00:03:35.544 --> 00:03:37.410
- In concert in 1994.

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:38.340
I was like 14.

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:41.377
It was her big, it was like
her first tour in 25 years.

00:03:41.377 --> 00:03:42.210
- (Luke) Wow.

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:43.043
- Bragger.

00:03:43.043 --> 00:03:43.876
- I know.

00:03:43.876 --> 00:03:46.260
I I remember it vividly to this day.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:47.550
I mean, we sat high up.

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:48.990
I mean the tickets were very expensive.

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:50.147
- You were in the room!

00:03:50.147 --> 00:03:52.140
- I was in the room with Barbara.

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:53.760
- Yeah. I've never been in the room.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:54.930
That's amazing.

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:55.860
- It was amazing.

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:57.780
- Yeah. Oh my gosh.

00:03:57.780 --> 00:04:00.120
Billy, you're making
history with this movie

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:03.900
and it was almost an entirely
LGBTQ plus cast and crew.

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:06.270
So how does it feel now
that the movie's closer

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:07.103
to being released?

00:04:07.103 --> 00:04:09.450
Are you, I bet there's a
little bit of nerves involved.

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:10.283
- Of course.

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:11.329
I mean, you'd be crazy
not to be nervous, but--

00:04:11.329 --> 00:04:12.193
- Yeah.

00:04:12.193 --> 00:04:14.220
- But, you know, we all
love the movie so much.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.053
It's very rare.

00:04:15.053 --> 00:04:19.620
Almost the entire cast is
all openly LGBTQ actors,

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:21.480
even playing the straight characters,

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:22.800
which very rarely happens.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:24.709
Although, except for
some celebrity cameos.

00:04:24.709 --> 00:04:25.590
Thank you.

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:26.753
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:30.030
- We do have some very
fun celebrity cameos.

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:31.277
Deborah Messing from Will and Graces.

00:04:31.277 --> 00:04:32.110
- (Kelly) Oh my God, love her.

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:34.980
- Absolutely hilarious in this.

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:37.020
Kristin Chenoweth and a bunch of others.

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:38.220
I don't want to give it away.

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:39.870
But yeah, it was it was very special.

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:42.240
And you know, but a comedy
is a comedy, you know

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:44.100
it was produced by Judd Apatow,

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:46.069
who's made some of the
funniest comedies ever.

00:04:46.069 --> 00:04:46.902
- (Kelly) Yeah.

00:04:46.902 --> 00:04:48.330
- Bridesmaids and 40 year Old Virgin

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:50.252
and Knocked Up and Train Wreck.

00:04:50.252 --> 00:04:51.085
- (Kelly)Yeah.

00:04:51.085 --> 00:04:51.918
- And Nick Stahl directed it

00:04:51.918 --> 00:04:53.400
he made Forgetting Sarah Marshall.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:56.280
But we've never had a movie
like that, like a big, you know

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:58.735
studio comedy about gay couples.

00:04:58.735 --> 00:04:59.568
- (Luke)Yeah.

00:04:59.568 --> 00:05:00.401
And so that's what this is.

00:05:00.401 --> 00:05:02.070
But you know, if you're,
if you like comedy

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:02.903
you're gonna like it

00:05:02.903 --> 00:05:05.008
whether you're straight gay
or no matter what you are.

00:05:05.008 --> 00:05:05.841
- (Luke) Yeah.

00:05:05.841 --> 00:05:06.674
- Yeah. I It's just funny.

00:05:06.674 --> 00:05:07.507
Funny. It's

00:05:07.507 --> 00:05:08.340
- Funny. Yeah.

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:09.660
So, wait, so this was,

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:12.300
Luke this was your first time
auditioning for a studio film.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:13.133
Right?

00:05:13.133 --> 00:05:13.966
- It was my first time auditioning

00:05:13.966 --> 00:05:15.599
for a lead in a studio film.

00:05:15.599 --> 00:05:16.503
- (Kelly) Okay. A lead in a studio film.

00:05:16.503 --> 00:05:17.596
- Yes. Yes.

00:05:17.596 --> 00:05:18.429
- It went well.

00:05:18.429 --> 00:05:19.440
- It went well.

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:21.600
I, I'm still pinching myself.

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:22.433
Yeah, it's great.

00:05:22.433 --> 00:05:23.266
It's nerve-wrecking.

00:05:23.266 --> 00:05:25.920
I think, you know, as an
actor, you, you always

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:27.888
want to do the big movies,
but they seem so hard to get

00:05:27.888 --> 00:05:31.054
you know, the truth is it's
a very competitive business

00:05:31.054 --> 00:05:31.887
- (Kelly) Yeah.

00:05:31.887 --> 00:05:32.720
- As it turns out.

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:33.553
So yeah.

00:05:33.553 --> 00:05:34.386
I'm lucky it went well.

00:05:34.386 --> 00:05:35.370
And I'm lucky that a part came along

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:38.130
that just made so much
sense for me to inhabit.

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:39.135
- But speaking of parts of you also

00:05:39.135 --> 00:05:42.060
you play straight a lot,
on like Hallmark films.

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:42.900
- I do, yes.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:44.220
Hallmark has been very good to me

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:46.093
and I really enjoy working with Hallmark.

00:05:46.093 --> 00:05:46.926
- (Kelly) Yeah.

00:05:46.926 --> 00:05:49.290
- And yeah, I've made
about 13 Hallmark movies.

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:50.571
A lot of Christmas movies.

00:05:50.571 --> 00:05:51.980
- (Kelly) Yeah.

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:53.700
- I mean it's all, it's all acting.

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:54.870
Everyone's acting regardless.

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:56.640
But what, how, what's y'all take

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:59.550
on people like, on representation,
you know what I'm saying?

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:01.710
So if people are gay,
playing a straight person

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:03.780
or straight playing a gay
person, what's your take on it?

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:05.130
- Well, I just saw this morning

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:07.380
Hallmark is doing a
Hanukkah movie this year

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:10.377
and I wasn't called and
I'm furious you know.

00:06:10.377 --> 00:06:12.240
- I am writing a stern letter.

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:15.000
- Yeah, please, please
write to them, okay.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:17.460
You know, look, I mean,
acting is an art form

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:19.170
you know, you know, it's not like,

00:06:19.170 --> 00:06:20.077
oh gay can only play gay

00:06:20.077 --> 00:06:22.392
and straight can only play straight.

00:06:22.392 --> 00:06:23.225
- (Kelly) Yeah.

00:06:23.225 --> 00:06:25.140
But you know, historically,

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:29.430
most of the high profile LGBTQ
roles we've seen in movies,

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:32.040
those roles are often played
by straight movie stars.

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:34.530
And some of them have
been amazing, you know

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:36.270
of course they've been magnificent.

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:39.168
But we would like an
opportunity to star movies too,

00:06:39.168 --> 00:06:40.001
you know.

00:06:40.001 --> 00:06:40.834
- (Kelly) Yeah.

00:06:40.834 --> 00:06:41.667
We've never really gotten that.

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:43.650
Especially in a big
funny comedy like this.

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:45.870
And so we're just trying to, you know

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:47.970
correct that imbalance a little bit

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:50.100
and give new people an
opportunity to shine.

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:50.933
- Yeah.

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:52.740
- I agree with that.

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:53.580
- Yeah.

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:56.340
- Well in the movie Billy's
character struggles to date.

00:06:56.340 --> 00:06:58.440
So have either of you
really had a terrible date?

00:06:58.440 --> 00:06:59.883
You're lying if you say no.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:01.680
- Oh, definitely, yeah.

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:03.060
- Yeah.

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:04.962
- I had a date recently
where the guy worked

00:07:04.962 --> 00:07:08.430
for a Cannabis company,
which is totally fine.

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:09.480
Yeah. I'm like, what's the problem?

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:11.040
- No, no, no.

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:11.983
I think I heard a yeah!

00:07:11.983 --> 00:07:15.720
- Yeah, but, well he just
showed up extremely high.

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:16.553
- Oh, no.

00:07:16.553 --> 00:07:17.520
- Like extremely stoned

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:19.410
and made it impossible to communicate.

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:20.340
You know what I mean.

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:21.690
- Yeah. It was Seth Rogen .

00:07:24.962 --> 00:07:26.760
- But you know, dating is tough.

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:28.170
That's what we deal with in the movie.

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:29.337
Like, our characters are
both almost competing

00:07:29.337 --> 00:07:33.210
when they meet to see who's
more emotionally unavailable.

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:34.467
- Yeah.

00:07:34.467 --> 00:07:35.970
